cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AD Library Benchmarks"
message: "If you use these benchmarks or refer to their results, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Xcelerit Computing Ltd."
    website: "https://www.xcelerit.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/auto-differentiation/ad-benchmarks"
url: "https://github.com/auto-differentiation/ad-benchmarks"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible C++ benchmark suite comparing automatic differentiation
  libraries (XAD, CppAD, Adept 2, autodiff, ddx) against finite-difference
  baselines on four quantitative-finance workloads: Heston stochastic
  volatility Monte Carlo, SABR vol-surface calibration, XVA CVA on a
  swap portfolio, and a LIBOR market model swaption portfolio.
keywords:
  - automatic differentiation
  - adjoint methods
  - AAD
  - benchmark
  - quantitative finance
  - Monte Carlo
  - XVA
  - XAD
license: MIT
